'''Casual Duel Cup''' is a 1on1 non-eliminating tournament meant for rookies and low/mid-skilled players. One can think of it as the Duel Edition of [[QuakeWorld MIX League]].

Signups are to be approved by the admin - we want to limit the tournament to lower-skilled players, coming mostly from the QML ranks. Signups are limited to 32 players, with rookie players taking the priority - meaning at some point top players will be put on a waiting list to see if they get a seeding. Seeding is based on the earlier results of the players, at the discretion of the admin.

A non-eliminating tournament structure ('''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swiss-system_tournament#Accelerated_pairings Swiss with accelerated pairings]''') will be used. This means everyone gets to play the same amount of matches, even if one loses all their matches. The acceleration in this tournament is implemented by giving the top half of the players a free win against the bottom half of the players on the first round. 5 rounds of matches will be played, in addition to the first accelerated round. If the number of players in a round is not even, a bye will be awarded. After the swiss rounds, a single-elimination bracket is played, where the top 8 scoring players of the swiss will fight to be the '''Champ o'Da Cup'''.

All matches are Best of 5 (BO5).

== Format ==
* '''Accelerated Swiss''' into a '''Top 8 Single Elimination'''
* All matches are BO5.
* 5+3 rounds of matches, 1 match per week.
* No divisions, no regions.
* First round of pairings will be posted sometime early april!

