== Rules ==
* Don't be a dick.
* Don't cheat. You ''know'' '''THEY ''ARE''''' watching.

* Schedule rules: Schedule your games fast, and play them as soon as possible. Pairings are usually posted on Sunday, and the deadline is the next Sunday. In cases where a schedule can't be made, contact an admin. Preference is to make scheduling on the private '''#cdc-players-only''' channel for the sake of bookkeeping. Post your agreed upon date and time to the '''#cdc-scheduled''' channel.

* Ping rules: Find a server that keeps both players around the same ping +/- 13ms, if no such server can be found, the lower ping player will have to use '''cl_delay_packet''' to get closer to the higher ping player. '''No player needs to use cl_delay_packet to go over 64ms ping''', even if this means unequal pings for the players.
** Games are to be played on '''EU servers'''. Other servers can also be used, '''if both players agree'''.
*** If '''no agreement''' can be made, use UK/IE (dm6.uk) servers, '''regardless of ping'''.
*** Other plausible options for EU vs. Americas games could be NY (ny.quake.world) or Portugal (lisbon.qlash.com.br) servers.

* Settings: Standard settings by typing "/1on1" | To add match tag: "'''/1on1 CDC'''"
* Pause rules: Each player is allowed one pause per match, once you have used a pause and use it again, you have forfeited the map.
* Late rules: 15 minutes late from a match is a Walk Out and the win is awarded to the other player. If this happens a second time it's only 5 minutes and W/O + plausibly kicked out of tournament unless for very pressing reasons.

* Map rules:
** Toss (remove) two maps from the pool in the beginning of match.
** Use /cmd rnd to decide who gets to choose first (Player 1).
** Order: P1 toss map → P2 toss map → P1 pick map → losing player picks next.
** “Losing player” means the one trailing in total maps (0-1, 0–2 or 1-2). If tied (1–1), the one who lost the previous map.
** A map cannot be played twice.

* Client: ezquake 3.6.x. or unezquake 1.3.x. For your own sake, update your client!
** Remember to check with "f_version"

* Ruleset(ezquake): smackdown
* unezquake settings: If using unezquake: F_ruleset check's must report CLEAR in ruleset check
** Remember to check with "f_ruleset check"

* cl_idrive is NOT allowed, turn off your hardware SOCD functions if you have them.

* Reporting: send screenshots in [https://discord.gg/hT6mgwxP QML discord] [https://discord.com/channels/1306206890115469443/1463462011873525895 #cdc-reports] channel, a screenshot from [https://hub.quakeworld.nu/ hub] is preferred. '''Winner''' of the match does the report. Note that if either player /breaks a game it does not show up in hub!

* In disputed ruling cases, contact an admin.
